# Vault rules

This vault is Claude's long-term memory across sessions and repositories, and the
home of its configuration. Notes are plain Markdown with YAML frontmatter.

## Layout

| Folder | Holds | Used by Claude as |
|---|---|---|
| `memory/` | One durable fact per file, plus the recall index `MEMORY.md` | auto-memory of every project |
| `knowledge/` | Findings that outlive one project | notes |
| `projects/` | One note per project: state, branches, open tickets | notes |
| `decisions/` | Dated records of choices and rejected alternatives | notes |
| `agents/` | Subagent definitions | `~/.claude/agents` |
| `commands/` | Slash commands | `~/.claude/commands` |
| `scripts/hooks/` | Hook scripts registered in `settings.json` | `~/.claude/hooks` |
| `scripts/bin/` | Helper programs | `~/.claude/bin` |
| `workflow/CLAUDE.md` | How Claude works: routes, team, review, verification | `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` |
| `project-agents/<set>/` | Agents for one project; global on a PC that lists the set in `~/.claude/global-agent-sets` | linked per project by the Claude Configuration app |

`agents/`, `commands/`, `scripts/` and `workflow/` are live configuration, not notes. Put no
notes there: every Markdown file in `agents/` or `commands/` becomes an agent or a
command.

## When to write

Write a note only if the fact outlives the session, cannot be derived from code or
history, and saves real work next time. Search the vault first and extend an
existing note instead of adding a second one. Never store credentials, transcripts
or chat summaries.

## memory/

Every file holds one fact with this frontmatter:

```yaml
---
name: kebab-case-slug          # equals the file name
description: one line, used to decide relevance during recall
metadata:
  type: user | feedback | project | reference
---
```

Add one line per memory to `memory/MEMORY.md`.
